<title>PAKISTAN: CRICKET-PAKISTAN BEAT ZIMBABWE IN THIRD ONE-DAY MATCH.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-PAKISTAN BEAT ZIMBABWE IN THIRD ONE-DAY MATCH.</headline>
<dateline>PESHAWAR, Pakistan 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan beat Zimbabwe by 77 runs in their third and last one-day cricket international on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scores: Pakistan 264-9 in 40 overs (Ijaz Ahmad 117, Azam Khan 72; E.Matambanadzo 4-32). Zimbabwe, set a target of 225 in 34 overs due to crowd trouble, were 147 all out in 32.1 overs.</p>
<p>Pakistan won the series 3-0.</p>
